Thanks Simon. 

The problem turned out to be that the package RWeka was not loaded despite the 
line re.eval("library(RWeka)") in my code. I am not exactly sure why it is not 
loaded (I'm running windows 7 and R-2.12.2) but by printing out the result of 
search() (after re.eval("library(RWeka)") I can see that RWeka is not among the 
loaded packages. 

More generally, the problem seems to be that my personal library of R packages 
is not found automatically. My solution was to set the .libPaths() to include my 
personal library of R packages, i.e. I did:

re.eval(".libPaths(\"C:/Users/MyUserName/Documents/R/win-library/2.12\")");
re.eval("library(RWeka)");

Then it worked.

Best,
Mattias

