Dear all,

we have the problem, that adding a (up to now dummy) C source file to
our rJava based package leads to separate checks for each architecture
on CRAN, which will fail for arch='ppc':
http://www.r-project.org/nosvn/R.check/r-devel-macosx-ix86/gMCP-00check.html

loading checks for arch 'ppc'
** checking whether the package can be loaded ... ERROR
Loading required package: graph
Loading required package: rJava
Loading required package: MASS
Loading required package: PolynomF
Java for ppc cannot run in this configuration.
Please consult documentation.
Error : .onLoad failed in loadNamespace() for 'gMCP', details:
call: .jinit()
error: Cannot create Java virtual machine (-1)
Error: package/namespace load failed for 'gMCP'
Execution halted

(Without the C file, CRAN provides the package also for MacOS X.)

So since I am totally unfamiliar with this problem and do not own a Mac:
Is rJava not working that way on arch='ppc' or is CRAN misconfigured
or am I doing something wrong and is there a way to fix that? (Also
other rJava based projects on CRAN with C files seem to have the same
problem.)
Or is there a way to check for architectures with these problems and
disable calls to rJava there?
(Since the functionality of the package is fully usable also without
the Java GUI.)

Or am totally on the wrong track? ;)

Thanks and best regards, Kornelius.

From simon.urbanek at r-project.org  Tue Mar 22 14:02:52 2011
From: simon.urbanek at r-project.org (Simon Urbanek)
