Message-ID: <9E1BA1C1-D83A-4B48-94CB-8B68758BFDEB@r-project.org>

Kornelius,

the issue has to do with Apple updates - they no longer support Java in Rosetta (for a while, actually) so unfortunately ppc checks cannot be run if they include Java. I think the most reliable solution for me is to disable checks on ppc. Given that we did not run separate checks before and we may want to leave ppc behind in not-so-distant future, I think it's an acceptable solution. The next rounds of checks shall not include ppc so the package should go through as long as it passes on both Intel archs.

Thanks,
Simon


