Message-ID: <4576EE97-964E-48E9-849D-C0390AEA6312@r-project.org>

I bet that's because your JRI.DLL is 32-bit -- easy to check-run R on the command line and you'll see:

> .jengine(T)
Cannot find JRI native library!
Please make sure that the JRI native library is in a directory listed in java.library.path.

java.lang.UnsatisfiedLinkError: C:\Program Files\R\R-2.12.2\library\rJava\jri\jri.dll: Can't load IA 32-bit .dll on a AMD 64-bit platform


If that's the case, make sure you use the 64-bit version of JRI.DLL (either add x64 to the library path or copy the 64-bit version down).

Cheers,
Simon


